"hadiths[774]{hadithnumber,text}:"
2950,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Beware of narrating from me except what I taught you"
2951,"Narrated Jundab bin 'Abdullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever says (something) about the Qur'an according to his own opinion and he is correct"
2952,"Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: Ḥammād ibn Yaḥyya al-Abaḥḥ narrated to us, from Thābit al-Bunānī, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said:

""The example of my Ummah is like the rain; it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end.""

He (the author) said: In this chapter, there are narrations from ʿAmmār, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr, and Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them all). This is a ḥasan gharīb Ḥadīth from this chain of narration.

It is also narrated that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī used to vouch for Ḥammād ibn Yaḥyya al-Abaḥḥ and would say: ""He is one of our shaykhs."""
2953,"Narrated 'Adiyy bin Hatim:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""The Jews are those who Allah is wrath with"
2954,"Narrated Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed Allah Most High created Adam from a handful that He took from all of the earth. So the children of Adam come in according with the earth"
2955,"Narrated by al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Khallal and others, who said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, saying: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with both of them), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said:

""Verily, the people are like a hundred camels; a man can scarcely find among them a single mount (i.e., one suitable for riding).""

Abu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: This is a hasan sahih hadith."
2956,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amir bin Rabi'ah:from his father who said: ""We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on a journey on a very dark night and we did not know where the Qiblah was. So each man among us prayed in his own direction. In the morning when we mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
2957,"Qutaybah narrated to us, who said: al-Mughirah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said:

""My example and the example of my Ummah is like that of a man who kindled a fire, and the flies and moths began to fall into it. I am holding you back by your waistbands, while you are plunging into it.""

He (the narrator) said: This is a hasan sahih hadith, and it has been narrated through multiple chains."
2958,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would perform voluntary Salat upon his mount facing whichever direction he was headed"
2959,"Narrated Anas:that 'Umar bin Al-Khattab said: ""O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! I wish that we could perform Salat behind the Maqam: So the following was revealed: And take you the Maqam of Ibrahim as a place of Salat. (2:)"
2960,"Narrated Anas:that 'Umar bin Al-Khattab [may Allah be pleased with him] said: ""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! I wish that you could perform Salat behind the Maqam of Ibrahim.' So the following was revealed: And take you the Maqam of Ibrahim as a place of Salat"
2961,"Narrated Abu Sa'eed:that about Allah's saying: Thus we have made you a Wasata nation (2:143) - the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""The meaning of Wasata is just."" [Abu 'Eisa said: This Hadith is [Hasan] Sahih. (Another chain) From Abu Sa'eed who narrated that: ""The Messenger of Allah a said: 'Nuh will be called and it will be said: ""Did you deliver (the Message)? ""He will say: ""Yes"" and his people will be called and it will be said: ""Did he call you?"" They will say: ""No warner came to us. No one came to us.' It will be said: ""Who will testify for you?"" So it is said: ""Muhammad and his Ummah (community)."" He (ﷺ) said: You will be brought to testify that he delivered (the Message) and that is His saying: Thus"
2962,"Narrated Al-Bara bin 'Azib:""When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) arrived in Al-Madinah"
2963,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us, he said:** Abū Aḥmad narrated to us, he said: Sufyān narrated to us, from Ibn Abī Laylā, from his brother, ʿĪsā, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī رضي الله عنه, that he had a storehouse in which there was dates, and a **ghūl** (a type of jinn or devil) used to come and take from it.

He said: So he complained about that to the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: **""Go, and when you see her, say: 'Bismillāh, ajībī Rasūl Allāh (In the Name of Allah, respond to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ).'""**

He said: So he seized her, and she swore that she would not return. He released her, and then came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who asked: **""What has your captive done?""** He replied: She swore that she would not return. The Prophet ﷺ said: **""She has lied, and she is one who is accustomed to lying.""**

He said: So he seized her a second time, and again she swore that she would not return. He released her and came to the Prophet ﷺ, who asked: **""What has your captive done?""** He replied: She swore that she would not return. The Prophet ﷺ said: **""She has lied, and she is one who is accustomed to lying.""**

He said: So he seized her and said: **""I shall not leave you until I bring you to the Prophet ﷺ.""** She said: **""I shall tell you something: Āyat al-Kursī — recite it in your home, and no devil (shayṭān) or any other creature shall come near you.""**

He said: So he came to the Prophet ﷺ, who asked: **""What has your captive done?""** He informed him of what she had said. The Prophet ﷺ said: **""She has spoken the truth, even though she is a liar.""**

---

**This is a ḥasan gharīb hadith.** There are narrations on this topic from Ubayy ibn Kaʿb رضي الله عنه."
2964,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""When the Prophet (ﷺ) began facing the Ka'bah they said: 'O Messenger of Allah! How about our brothers who died while they were praying toward Bait Al-Maqdis?' So Allah Most High revealed: Allah would not allow your faith to be wasted. (2:)"
2965,"Narrated Az-Zuhri:that 'Urqah said: ""I said to 'Aishah: 'I do not see anything wrong if someone does not go between As-Safa and Al-Marwah"
2966,"Narrated 'Asim Al-Ahwal:""I asked Anas bin Malik about As-Safa and Al-Marwah"
2967,"Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:""When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) arrived in Makkah"
2968,"Narrated Al-Bara bin 'Azib:""It was the custom among the Companions of Muhammad (ﷺ)"
2969,Narrated An-Nu'man bin Bashir:from the Prophet (ﷺ) regarding Allah's saying: Your Lord said: Invoke Me
2970,"Narrated 'Adi bin Hatim:""When 'Until the white (light) thread of dawn appears distinct to you from the black thread (of night)' was revealed"
2971,"Narrated 'Adi bin Hatim:""I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the fast"
2972,"Narrated Aslam bin 'Imran At-Tujibi:""We were in a Roman city, when a large column of Romans came out to us. So about the same number or more of the Muslims went towards them. The commander of the people of Egypt was 'Uqbah bin 'Amir, and the commenter of the (our) group was Fadalah bin 'Ubaid. One man among the Muslims reached the Roman line until he entered amidst them, so the people started screaming: 'Subhan Allah! He has thrown himself into destruction!' Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari said: 'O you people! You give this interpretation for this Ayah, while this Ayah was only revealed about us, the people among the Ansar, when Allah made Islam might, and increased its supporters. Some of us secretly said to each other, outside of the presence of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): ""Our wealth has been ruined, and Allah has strengthened Islam, and increased its supporters, so if we tend to our wealth then what we lost of it shall be revitalized for us."" So Allah, Blessed and Most High, revealed to His Prophet (ﷺ), rebuking what we said: 'And spend in the cause of Allah, and do not throw yourselves into destruction. (2:195)' So the destruction was tending to the wealth and maintaining it.' Abu Ayyub did not cease traveling in Allah's cause, until he was buried in the land of the Romans."""
2973,"Narrated Mujahid:that Ka'b bin 'Ujrah said: ""By the one in Whose Hand is my soul! This Ayah was revealed referring to my case: 'And whosoever of you is ill or has an ailment on his scalp (necessitating shaving) he must pay Fidyah of either fasting or giving charity"
2974,"Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Abi Laila:from Ka'b bin 'Ujrah who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to me while I was lighting a fire under a pot"
2975,"Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Ya'mar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The Hajj is 'Arafat"
2976,"Narrated 'Aishah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The most hated man to Allah is the most quarrelsome"
2977,"**Narrated by Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with both of):**

The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""When Az-Zilzal (Surah 99) is recited, it is equal to half of the Qur'an, and Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad (Surah 112) is equal to one-third of the Qur'an, and Qul Ya Ayyuhal-Kafirun (Surah 109) is equal to one-quarter of the Qur'an.""

Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: This is a gharib (uncommon) hadith; we do not know it except through the narration of Yaman ibn al-Mughirah."
2978,"Narrated Jabir:""The Jews would say: ""Whoever goes into his wife's vagina from behind her"
2979,"# Hadith of Surah Al-Ikhlas Being Equal to One-Third of the Qur'an

**Narrated by Awfa ibn Malik** (may Allah be pleased with him):

Qutaybah and Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, they both said: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Za'idah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Rabi' ibn Khuthaym, from 'Amr ibn Maymun, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from a woman — she being the wife of Abu Ayyub — from Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:

The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:

**""Is it not within the ability of any one of you to recite one-third of the Qur'an in a single night?""**

He ﷺ then said: **""Reciting *Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad* (Surah Al-Ikhlas) constitutes one-third of the Qur'an.""**

---

**Sub-narrators (Taba'at):** There are narrations on this topic from Abu al-Darda', Abu Sa'id, Qatadah ibn al-Nu'man, Abu Hurayrah, Anas, Ibn 'Umar, and Abu Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with them all).

---

**Imam Abu 'Isa al-Tmidhi's commentary (rahimahullah):**

""This is a *hasan* (good) hadith. We do not know of anyone who narrated this hadith in a more excellent manner than the narration of Za'idah. Israel and al-Fudayl ibn 'Iyyad followed him upon his narration. Shu'bah and a number of trustworthy narrators also transmitted this hadith from Mansur, though they exhibited some variance (idtirab) in it.""

---

*Related by al-Tirmidhi in his Sunan, Kitab Fada'il al-Qur'an.*"
2980,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""'Umar came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! I am ruined!' He said: 'Why are you ruined?' He said: 'I turned my mount during the night (meaning that he went into his wife from behind).'"" He said: ""So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not say anything in reply to him. Then Allah revealed this Ayah to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): 'Your wives are a tilth for you"
2981,Narrated Al-Hasan:from Ma'qil bin Yasar that he married his sister to a man among the Muslims during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). She remained with him as long as she did
2982,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him):**

The Messenger of Allāh, peace and blessings be upon him, said:

> **""Say: He is Allāh, the One"" (Sūrah al-Ikhlāṣ, 112:1) is equivalent to one-third of the Qurʾān.**

This is a *ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ* hadith.

---

## Chain of Narration (Isnād)

- **Al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dawrī** narrated to us, saying:
- **Khālid ibn Makhlad** narrated to us, saying:
- **Sulaymān ibn Bilāl** narrated to us, saying:
- **Suhayl ibn Abī Ṣāliḥ** narrated to us, from his father (Abū Ṣāliḥ), from **Abū Hurayrah** (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said: the Messenger of Allāh, peace and blessings be upon him, said…

---

## Scholarly Notes

This hadith establishes the immense virtue of **Sūrah al-Ikhlāṣ** (Qurʾān 112), affirming that its recitation carries the reward equivalent to one-third of the entire Qurʾān. This is understood by scholars to refer to the Sūrah's comprehensive encapsulation of **Tawḥīd** (Divine Oneness), which constitutes one of the three fundamental themes of the Qurʾān: **Tawḥīd** (monotheism), **Sharīʿah** (legislation), and **Akhīrah** (the Hereafter). Thus, Sūrah al-Ikhlāṣ, being a pure and unadulterated declaration of Divine Unity, is deemed equivalent in spiritual weight to one-third of the Book of Allāh, exalted is He."
