3031,"Narrated Al-Bara bin 'Azib:""When the following was revealed: 'Not equal are those of the believers who sit (4:95)' 'Amr bin Umm Maktum came to the Prophet (ﷺ)."" He said: ""He was blind"
3032,"# Hadith Translation

## Ḥadīth No. 2939 — On the Recitation of the Qur'ān

**Narrated by 'Abdullāh ibn 'Amr (may Allāh be pleased with him):**

The Prophet ﷺ said:

**""He who recites the Qur'ān in less than three days does not understand it.""**

---

### Chain of Transmission (Isnād)

**Narrated to us Maḥmūd ibn Ghaylān** — he said: **Narrated to us** **al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl** — he said: **Narrated to us Shu'bah**, from **Qatādah**, from **Yazīd ibn 'Abdullāh ibn al-Shikhkhīr**, from **'Abdullāh ibn 'Amr** (may Allāh be pleased with him) that the Prophet ﷺ said:

**""He who recites the Qur'ān in less than three days does not understand it.""**

---

### Grading

**Abū 'Īsā (al-Tirmidhī, raḥimahullāh) said:** *""This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ ḥadīth.""*

---

### Corroborating Narration

**Narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Bashshār** — he said: **Narrated to us Muḥammad ibn Ja'far** — he said: **Narrated to us Shu'bah**, with **this isnād**, a similar narration.

---

### Scholarly Notes

- **Reference:** *Jāmi' al-Tirmidhī*, Book of Virtues of the Qur'ān (Bāb Fī Fī Faḍl al-Qur'ān), Ḥadīth no. 2939.
- **Meaning:** The ḥadīth indicates that one who rushes through the entire Qur'ān in fewer than three days fails to grasp its deeper meanings, for proper *tilāwah* (recitation) requires contemplation (*tadabbur*), reflection, and measured pacing. The prohibition here pertains to haste that precludes comprehension, not merely the speed of recitation in itself.
- **Source:** Sunan al-Tirmidhī, Kitāb al-Qur'ān 'an Rasūlillāh ﷺ."
3033,"Narrated Ya'la bin Umayyah:""I said to 'Umar [bin Al-Khattab]: 'Allah said: That you shorten the Salat if you fear and the people are safe (4:101).' So 'Umar said: 'I wondered about that just as you have wondered. So I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
3034,Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) halted between Dajnan and 'Usfan
3035,"Narrated Qatadah bin An-Nu'man:""There was a household among us called Banu Ubairiq"
3036,"Narrated Thuwair - Ibn Abi Fakhitah:from his father that 'Ali bin Abi Talib said: ""There is no Ayah in the Qur'an more beloved to me than this Ayah: Verily Allah forgives not associating others with Him"
3037,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:""When the following was revealed: 'Whoever works evil will have the recompense of it... (4:123)' That worried the Muslims"
3038,"Narrated Abu Bakr As-Siddiq:""I was with the Prophet (ﷺ) when this Ayah was revealed to him: Whoever works evil will have the recompense of it (4:123). So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'O Abu Bakr! Shall I recite to you an Ayah revealed to me?' I said: 'Of course O Messenger of Allah!' So he recited it to me"
3039,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""Sawdah feared that the Prophet (ﷺ) was going to divorce her"
3040,"Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from Ma'mar, from Hammam ibn Munabbih, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said regarding His (Exalted is He) words: ""Enter the gate prostrating"" (Qur'an 2:58), he said: ""They entered dragging themselves on their buttocks."" And with this chain of narration from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) regarding His words: ""But the wrongdoers changed the word from that which had been said to them"" (Qur'an 2:59), he said: ""They said: 'A grain in a hair.'"" Abu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: This is a hasan sahih hadith."
3041,"Narrated Al-Bara:""A man came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! They ask you about a legal verdict. Say: ""Allah directs (thus) regarding Al-Kalalah (4:176)."" So the Prophet (ﷺ) said to him: ""You should be sufficed with the Ayah of summer."" (Meaning this Ayah"
3042,"Narrated Tariq bin Shihab:""A man among the Jews said to 'Umar bin Al-Khattab: 'O Commander of the Believers! If we were the ones unto whom this Ayah was revealed"
3043,"Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated from Humayd, from Anas"
3044,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Ar-Rahman's Hand is full"
3045,"Narrated 'Aishah:""The Prophet (ﷺ) was being guarded until this Ayah was revealed: 'Allah will protect you from mankind.' So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stuck his head out from the room and said: 'O you people! Go away"
3046,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'When the Children of Isra'il fell into disobedience"
3047,"Narrated Abu 'Ubaidah:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'When the Children of Isra'il fell into decline"
3048,Narrated 'Amr bin Shurahbil [Abu Maisarah]:from 'Umar bin Al-Khattab
3049,"Narrated Al-Bara:""A man among the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) died before Khamr had been made unlawful. So when Khamr was made unlawful"
3050,"Narrated Al-Bara bin 'Azib:""Some people among the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) died while they had been drinking Khamr. So when it was revealed that it was unlawful"
3051,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""They (the Companions) said: 'O Messenger of Allah"
3052,"Narrated 'Abdullah:""When (the following) was revealed: Those who believe and do righteous good deeds"
3053,"Narrated 'Ikrimah:from Ibn 'Abbas: ""A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! When I consume meat and I get around women"
3054,"Narrated Abu Al-Bukhtari:from 'Ali who said: ""When (the following) was revealed: And Hajj to the House is a duty that mankind owes to Allah"
3055,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:that a man said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Who is my father?"" He said: ""Your father is so-and-so."" He said: ""So (the following) was revealed: O you who believe! Ask not about things which"
3056,"Narrated Abu Bakr As-Siddiq:""O you people! You recite this Ayah: Take care of yourselves! If you follow the guidance no harm shall come to you from those who are astray (5:105). I indeed heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: 'When the people see the wrongdoer"
3057,"Narrated Abu Umayah Ash-Sha'bani:""I went to Abu Tha'balah Al-Khushani and said to him: 'How do you deal with this Ayah?' He said: 'Which Ayah?' I said: 'Allah's saying: Take care of yourselves! If you follow the guidance no harm shall come to you (5:105).' He said: 'Well"
3058,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated Ka'b ibn 'Ujrah (may Allah be pleased with him):**

He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came upon me while I was kindling a fire beneath a cooking pot, and lice were falling upon my forehead — or he said, upon my eyebrows. So he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: **""Do the vermin of your head harm you?""**

He said: I replied, ""Yes.""

He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: **""Then shave your head, and offer a sacrifice, or fast three days, or feed six poor persons.""**

Ayyub (one of the narrators) said: ""I do not know with which of the three he began.""

Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: **This is a hasan sahih hadith.**

---

*This narration is recorded in Jami' al-Tirmidhi and is also found in the collections of al-Bukhari and Muslim. It pertains to the rulings of Hajj and Umrah, specifically the expiation (fidyah) required for one who is in the state of ihram and is compelled to remove head lice or shave due to severe harm.*"
3059,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""A man from Banu Sahm went out with Tamim Ad-Dari and 'Adi bin Badda. The Sahmi man died in a land in which there were no Muslims. When they arrived with what he left behind"
3060,"Narrated 'Ammar bin Yasir:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'The Ma'idah was sent down from the Heavens with bread and meat. And they were commanded to not be deceitful with it and hide it for tomorrow. So they were deceitful with it and they hid it"
3061,"# Translation of the Hadith

Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to me, Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us from Thābit, from Anas رضي الله عنه, who said:

""The Jews, when a woman among them menstruated, would not eat with her, nor drink with her, nor cohabit with her in the houses. The Prophet ﷺ was asked about that, so Allah, the Most High, revealed: *'They ask you about menstruation. Say: It is a harm (adha).'* (Al-Baqarah: 222)

So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded them to eat with them (menstruating women), to drink with them, and to remain with them in the houses, and to do everything except sexual intercourse.

The Jews then said: 'He does not wish to leave anything of our practice except that he opposes us in it.'""

Anas رضي الله عنه said: ""Then ʿAbbād ibn Bishr and Usayd ibn Ḥuḍayr رضي الله عنهما came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him of that, and they said: 'O Messenger of Allah, should we not then have intercourse with them during menstruation?' The face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed (his expression altered) until we thought that he had become angry with them. So they left. Then a gift of milk was presented, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent someone after them and gave them to drink, so we knew that he had not been angry with them.""

Abu ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: ""This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith.""

---

**Note:** This hadith is recorded in *Sunan al-Tirmidhī* and also appears in *Ṣaḥīḥ Muslim*. It illustrates the Islamic ruling regarding the treatment of menstruating women, the prohibition of sexual intercourse during menses, and the Prophet's ﷺ gentle correction of his Companions when they misunderstood his reaction."
3062,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr:""The last Surah revealed was Surat Al-Ma'idah and Al-Fath"
3063,"Narrated 'Ali:""Abu Jahl said to the Prophet (ﷺ): 'We do not deny you"
3064,"Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:""When Allah revealed this Ayah: 'Say: He has the power to send torment on you from above or from under your feet...' The Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'I seek refuge in Your Face.' So when (the following) was revealed: 'Or to cover you in confusion in party strife"
3065,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by 'Abd ibn Humayd** — who said: **Hisham ibn al-Qasim** narrated to us — from **al-Mubarak ibn Fadalah** — from **al-Hasan** — from **Ma'qil ibn Yasar** (may Allah be pleased with him):

---

That he gave his sister in marriage to a man from among the Muslims during the era of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She remained with him for a time, after which he divorced her with a single divorce and did not take her back until her waiting period ('iddah) had expired. Then both he and she developed a mutual longing for one another. Subsequently, he sought her hand in marriage along with other suitors. Ma'qil (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: ""O wretched fellow! I honoured you by giving her to you in marriage, and you divorced her! By Allah, she shall never return to you!"" The final word was his.

Then Allah, Exalted is He, knew of his need for her and of her need for a husband, so Allah revealed:

> **""And when you have divorced women and they have reached their prescribed term…""** — until His statement: **""…while you do not know.""** (al-Baqarah, 2:231)

When Ma'qil (may Allah be pleased with him) heard the verse, he said: ""I hear and obey my Lord."" Then he called the man and said: ""I give her to you in marriage and I honour you.""

---

**Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi, may Allah have mercy upon him)** said: *""This is a hasan sahih hadith. It has been narrated through other chains from al-Hasan. In this hadith there is evidence that marriage without a guardian (wali) is not permissible, for the sister of Ma'qil ibn Yasar was a previously married woman (thayyib), and had the matter been in her hands without her guardian, she would have married herself and would not have needed her guardian, Ma'qil ibn Yasar. Rather, Allah addressed the guardians in the first verse, saying:*

> **""…and do not prevent them from marrying their husbands…""** (al-Baqarah, 2:33)

*In this verse there is evidence that the matter of marriage rests with the guardians, together with the women's consent.""*

---

*Related by al-Tirmidhi (may Allah have mercy upon him), who graded it hasan sahih.*"
3066,"Narrated 'Abdullah:""When (the following) was revealed: It is those who believe and confuse not their belief with Zulm (wrong) (6:82) - That bothered some Muslims"
3067,"Narrated Masruq:""I was reclining in the presence of 'Aishah when she said: 'O Abu 'Aishah! There are three things"
3068,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Abbas:""Some people came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and they said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Why is it that we can eat what we kill but we can not eat what Allah has killed?' So Allah revealed: So eat of that on which Allah's Name has been mentioned if you are indeed believers in His Ayat..."" up to His saying: ...And if you obey them"
3069,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud:""Whoever wishes to look at the Sahifah which Muhammad (ﷺ) placed his seal upon"
3070,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him):**

Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated to us, who said: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah, Yazid ibn Harun, and Muhammad ibn 'Ubaid narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Harith ibn Shubayl, from Abu 'Amr al-Shaybani, from Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:

""We used to speak during the prayer in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), until the verse was revealed: **'And stand before Allah in devout obedience'** (al-Baqarah, 2:238). We were then commanded to observe silence.""

Ahmad ibn Mani' also narrated to us, who said: Hushaym narrated to us, who said: Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us a similar narration, and he added therein: **""and we were forbidden from speaking.""**

Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: **""This is a hasan sahih hadith. And Abu 'Amr al-Shaybani's name is Sa'd ibn Iyas.""**

---

*This hadith establishes the prohibition of speaking during the prayer (ṣalāh), as mandated by the Qur'anic injunction to stand before Allah in devout obedience (qānitīn), which the Companions understood as a command to maintain silence and reverence during the prayer.*"
3071,
3072,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Allah"
3073,"Narrated Sulaiman bin Harb:""Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us"
3074,Narrated Muslim bin Yasar Al-Juhani:that 'Umar bin Al-Khattab was asked about this Ayah: And when your Lord brought forth from the Children of Adam
3075,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""When Allah created Adam He wiped his back and every person that He created among his offspring until the Day of Resurrection fell out of his back. He placed a ray of light between the eyes of every person. Then He showed them to Adam and he said: 'O Lord! Who are these people?' He said: 'These are your offspring.' He saw one of them whose ray between his eyes amazed him"
3076,"Narrated Samurah bin Jundab:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""When Hawwa became pregnant"
3077,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""When Allah created Adam"" (and he mentioned) the Hadith"
3078,"Narrated Mus'ab bin Sa'd:from his father who said: ""On the Day of Badr I brought a sword so I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Indeed Allah has satisfied my breast (i.e. my desire) on the idolaters - or something like that - give me this sword.' So he said: 'This is not for me"
3079,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was finished at Badr"
3080,"# Hadith Translation

**It was narrated to us by Hannād, who narrated to us from Abū Mu'āwiyah, from al-A'mash, from Shaqīq ibn Salamah, from 'Abdullāh (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said:**

The Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) said:

> **""Whoever takes an oath upon a falsehood in order to usurp the wealth of a Muslim, he shall meet Allāh while He is angry with him.""**

Al-Ash'ath ibn Qays (may Allāh be pleased with him) said: ""By Allāh, that was concerning me. There was a dispute between myself and a Jewish man over a piece of land. He denied my claim, so I brought him before the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). The Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) said to me: **'Do you have proof?'** I said: 'No.' So he said to the Jew: **'Take an oath.'** I said: 'O Messenger of Allāh, if he swears, he will take away my property!' Then Allāh, the Blessed and Most High, revealed:

> **'Indeed, those who exchange the covenant of Allāh and their oaths for a small price…'** (Āl 'Imrān, 3:77) — until the end of the verse.

Abū 'Īsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: **""This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith.""** And there are narrations on this topic from Ibn Abī Awfā (may Allāh be pleased with him)."
3081,"Narrated to us Ishaq ibn Mansur, who narrated to us Abdullah ibn Bakr al-Sahmi, who narrated to us Humayd, from Anas رضي الله عنه, who said:

When this verse was lan: **""Never will you attain [true] righteousness until you spend [in charity] from that which you love""** (Aal-‘Imran 3:92) — or, **""Who is it that would loan to Allah a goodly loan so He may multiply it for him many times over?""** (Al-Baqarah 2:245) — Abu Talhah رضي الله عنه, who possessed a garden (ḥā’iṭ), said: *""O Messenger of Allah صلى الله عليه وسلم, my garden is for Allah. Had I been able to conceal it, I would never have disclosed it.""*

The Prophet صلى الله عليه وسلم said: **""Place it among your relatives and next of kin.""**

Abu ‘Isa [al-Tirmidhi] رحمه الله said: *""This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith. It has also been narrated by Malik ibn Anas from Ishaq ibn ‘Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah from Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه.""*

---

**Note:** This narration is recorded by Imam Abu ‘Isa al-Tirmidhi رحمه الله in his *Sunan*, and it is also transmitted through the chain of Imam Malik رحمه"
3082,"Narrated 'Uqbah bin 'Amir:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) recited this Ayah upon the Minbar: And make ready against them all you can of power (8:60). He said: ""Verily! Power is shooting"" - three times - ""Verily! Allah will open the earth for you and suffice you with supplies"
3083,"Narrated 'Amr bin Murrah:that Abu 'Ubaidah bin 'Abdullah narrated from 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud who said: ""On the Day of Badr"
3084,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""None of the black heads (meaning the Children of Adam since (most of) their heads are black) before you partook of spoils of war"
3085,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""I said to 'Uthman bin 'Affan: 'What was your reasoning with Al-Anfal - while it is from the Muthani (Surah with less than one-hundred Ayat)"
3086,"Narrated Sulaiman bin 'Amr bin Al-Ahwas:""My father narrated to me that he attended the Farewell Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He (ﷺ) expressed his gratitude to Allah and praised Him"
3087,"Narrated 'Ali:""I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the day of Al-Hajj Al-Akbar"
3088,"Narrated 'Ali:""The day of Al-Hajj Al-Akbar is the day of An-Nahr"
3089,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:""The Prophet (ﷺ) sent Abu Bakr with the (announcement of) Bara'ah (the declaration to publicize the disavowal of the idolaters). Then he summoned him and said: 'It is not right for anyone to convey this except a man among my family.'""So he called for 'Ali and gave it to him"
3090,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) dispatched Abu Bakr ordering him to announce these statements. Then 'Ali followed him. When Abu Bakr was at a particular road"
3091,"Narrated Zaid bin Yuthai':""We asked 'Ali what he had been dispatched with during the Hajj. He said: 'I was sent with four: That there shall be no Tawaf around the House while naked"
3092,"Narrated Abu Sa'eed:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""When you see a man frequenting the Masjid"
3093,"Narrated Thawban:""When (the following) was revealed: And those who hoard up gold and silver... (9:34)"" He said: ""We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) during one of his journeys"
3094,"Narrated 'Adi bin Hatim:""I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) while I had a cross of gold around my neck. He said: 'O 'Adi! Remove this idol from yourself!' And I heard him reciting from Surah Bara'ah: They took their rabbis and monks as lords besides Allah (9:31). He said: 'As for them"
3095,"Narrated by Ibn Abi 'Umar, narrated by Sufyan, from Al-A'mash, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from Masruq, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), that he was asked regarding the statement of Allah, the Most High: *""And never think of those who have been killed in the cause of Allah as dead. Rather, they are alive with their Lord, receiving provision.""* (Qur'an 3:169)

He (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Indeed, we asked about that, and we were informed that their souls are in green birds that roam freely in Paradise wherever they wish, and they take refuge in lanterns suspended beneath the Throne. Then your Lord looked upon them and said: 'Do you wish for anything more, that I may increase it for you?' They said: 'Our Lord, what more could we wish for when we are in Paradise, roaming wherever we please?' Then He looked upon them a second time and said: 'Do you wish for anything more, that I may increase it for you?' When they realized they would not be left without an answer, they said: 'Return our souls to our bodies so that we may return to the world and be killed again in Your cause.'""

Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: ""This is a hasan sahih hadith.""

Narrated by Ibn Abi 'Umar, narrated by Sufyan, from 'Atā' ibn al-Sā'ib, from Abū 'Ubaydah, from Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), with a similar narration, and he added in it: ""And convey peace to our Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and inform him that we are pleased, and He is pleased with us.""

Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: ""This is a hasan hadith."""
3096,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""I heard 'Umar bin Al-Khattab saying: 'When 'Abdullah bin Ubayy died"
3097,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:""'Abdullah bin 'Abdullah bin Ubayy came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when his father died"
3098,"Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:""Two men disagreed over the Masjid whose foundation was laid upon Taqwa from the first day (9:108). A man said: 'It is Masjid Quba' and the other said: 'It is the Masjid of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).' So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'It is this Masjid of mine"
3099,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""This Ayah was revealed about the people of Quba: In it are men who love to purify themselves. And Allah loves those who make themselves pure (9:108)."" He said: ""They used water to perform Istinja so this Ayah was revealed about them"
3100,"Narrated 'Ali:""I heard a man seeking forgiveness for his parents who were idolaters"
3101,"Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Ka'b bin Malik:from his father who said: ""I did not remain behind from any of the battles the Prophet (ﷺ) fought in"
3102,"Narrated by Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-A'la al-San'ani, from Khalid ibn al-Harith, from Shu'bah, from 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Anas, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), regarding the major sins, he (peace and blessings be upon him) said:

""Associating partners with Allah, disobedience to parents, taking a life, and false testimony.""

Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: This is a hasan gharib sahih hadith. It was also narrated by Ruh ibn 'Ubadah from Shu'bah, who reported it from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr, but that chain is not authentic."
3103,"Narrated Az-Zuhri:from Anas who said: ""Hudhaifah bin Al-Yaman came to 'Uthman"
3104,"Abdullah ibn Unays al-Juhani (may Allah be pleased with him) reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said:

""Indeed, among the greatest of major sins are: associating partners with Allah, disobedience to parents, and the false oath (al-yamin al-ghamus). And no one swears an oath by Allah—a deliberate oath—and includes in it even something as small as the wing of a mosquito, except that a black spot will be placed in his heart until the Day of Judgment.""

Abu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: ""Abu Umamah al-Ansari is Ibn Tha'labah, and we do not know his name. He narrated hadiths from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him).""

Abu Isa said: ""This is a hasan gharib hadith."""
3105,"Narrated 'Ata bin Yasar:from a man among the people of Egypt who said: ""I asked Abu Ad-Darda about this Ayah: For them is good news in the life of the present world (10:64). He said: 'No one asked me about since I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about it"
3106,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""When Allah drowned Fir'awn he said: 'I believe that there is no god except the One that the children of Isra'il believe in.' So Jibrail said: 'O Muhammad! If you could only have seen me"
3107,"Narrated Shu'bah:""'Adi bin Thabit and 'Ata bin As-Sa'ib informed me"
3108,"Narrated Waki' bin Hudus:from his uncle Abu Razin who said: ""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Where was our Lord before He created His creation?' He said: 'He was (above) the clouds - no air was under him"
3109,"Narrated Abu Musa:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed Allah Blessed and Most High gives respite (Yumli)"" and perhaps he said: ""(Yumhil)"" respite to the wrong-doer until"
3110,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that 'Umar bin Al-Khattab said: ""When this Ayah was revealed: Some among them will be wretches and (others) blessed (11:105). I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: 'O Prophet of Allah! Based upon what are we then working; something that has already finished or something that has not yet happened?' He said: 'Rather something that has happened"
3111,"Narrated 'Abdullah:""A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: 'I fondled a woman who lives on the edge of Al-Madinah"
3112,"Narrated Mu'adh bin Jabal:""A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! What do you say about a man who meets a woman and there is no acquaintance between them. So there is nothing that a man who would do with his wife but he does it with her"
3113,Narrated Ibn Mas'ud:that a man unlawfully kissed a woman. So he came to the Prophet (ﷺ) to ask him about its atonement. So (the following) Ayah was revealed: And perform the Salat
3114,"Narrated Musa bin Talhah:that Abu Al-Yasar said: ""A woman came to me selling dates. I said to her: 'There are better dates than these in the house.' So she entered the house with me. I had an urge for her so I began kissing her. I went to Abu Bakr and mentioned that to him"
3115,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed"
3116,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""The Jews came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: 'O Abul-Qasim! Inform us about the thunder"
3117,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) commented on: ""Some of them We make more excellent than others to eat (13:4)."" He said: ""The Daqal"
3118,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was brought a dish with unripe dates on it. He said: The parable of a goodly word is that of a goodly tree"
3119,Narrated Al-Bara:that regarding Allah's saying: Allah will keep firm those who believe
3120,
3121,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""There was a woman who performed Salat behind the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) who was the most beautiful among the people. Some of the people would go forward to the first line so as not to see her. Others would go back to the last line so when he would bow"
3122,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""There are seven gates of Jahannam: Among them a gate for whoever carries a sword against my Ummah."" Or he said: ""Against the Ummah of Muhammad"
3123,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Al-Hamdulillah is Umm Al-Qur'an and Umm Al-Kitab and the seven oft-repeated"
3124,"Narrated Ubayy bin Ka'b:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Allah has not revealed the likes of Umm Al-Kitab in the Tawrah"
3125,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:that regarding Allah's saying: We shall certainly call all of them to account. For all that they used to do (15:92 & 93). The Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""About saying La Ilaha Illallah"
3126,"Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Beware of the believer's intuition"
3127,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Umar:""I heard 'Umar bin Al-Khattab saying: 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Four before Zuhr"
3128,"Abd ibn Humaid narrated to us, that Yazid ibn Harun informed us, that Hammad ibn Salamah informed us from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, who said: Ibn Abbas recited: *""Today I have perfected for you your religion, completed My favour upon you, and have chosen for you Islam as your religion""* (Qur'an 5:3). A Jew was present with him, and he said: ""Had this verse been revealed to us, we would have taken its day as a festival."" Ibn Abbas said: ""Indeed, it was revealed on a day of festival — on a day of Jumu'ah (Friday) and the Day of Arafah."" Abu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: This is a hasan gharib hadith from the hadith of Ibn Abbas, and it is sahih."
3129,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""When I was taken on the Night of Isra I met Musa."" He described him saying: ""He was a man who was"" and I think he said: ""A thin man"
3130,Narrated Anas:that Al-Buraq was brought to the Prophet (ﷺ) on the Night of Isra
3131,"Narrated Ibn Buraidah:from his father that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""When we reached Bait Al-Maqdis"
3132,"Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""When the Quraish belied me"
3133,"Narrated by Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman, who reported from Muhammad ibn Yusuf, who reported from Isra'il, who narrated from Abu Ishaq, from 'Umar ibn Sharahil Abu Mayssarah, from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), that he said:

""O Allah, grant us a clear and healing explanation regarding wine."" Then the verse in Surah al-Baqarah was revealed: *""They ask you about wine and gambling...""* (2:219). 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was summoned and the verse was recited to him. He again said: ""O Allah, grant us a clear and healing explanation regarding wine."" Then the verse in Surah al-Nisa' was revealed: *""O you who believe, do not approach prayer while you are intoxicated...""* (4:43). 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was summoned and the verse was recited to him. He again said: ""O Allah, grant us a clear and healing explanation regarding wine."" Then the verse in Surah al-Ma'idah was revealed: *""Indeed, Satan intends to stir up enmity and hatred among you through wine and gambling...""* (5:91) until His words: *""So will you then desist?""* (5:91). 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was summoned and the verse was recited to him. He said: ""We have desisted, we have desisted.""

Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: This hadith has also been narrated from Isra'il in a mursal form. Muhammad ibn al-'Ala' narrated to us, saying: Waki' narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Mayssarah 'Amr ibn Sharahil, that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""O Allah, grant us a clear and healing explanation regarding wine..."" and he mentioned a similar narration. This version is more authentic than the hadith of Muhammad ibn Yusuf."
3134,"Narrated by al-Bara' (may Allah be pleased with he and his father): ""Some men among the Companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him) died before the prohibition of wine was revealed. When wine was prohibited, some people said, 'What about our companions who died while they drank it?' Then the following verse was revealed: 'Upon those who believed and did righteous deeds there is no sin for what they have eaten [in the past], if they fear Allah and believe and do righteous deeds.' (Quran 5:93).""

Abu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: ""This is a hasan sahih hadith."""
3135,"# Translation of the Hadith

It has also been narrated by Shuʿbah, from Abū Isḥāq, from al-Barāʾ. Muḥammad ibn Bashshār Bundār informed us of that; he said: Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, he said: Shuʿbah narrated to us, from Abū Isḥāq, with this chain. He said: al-Barāʾ ibn ʿāzib (may Allāh be pleased with him) said:

""A number of the Companions of the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa-sallam) died while they were drinking khamr (intoxicating wine). When the prohibition of it was revealed, some of the Companions of the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa-sallam) said: 'What about our companions who died while they were drinking it?' Thereupon the verse was revealed:

**'There is no blame upon those who believed and did righteous deeds…'** (al-Māʾidah 5:93) — the verse.""

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: ""This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith.""

---

*Note: This narration addresses the divine mercy extended to those Companions (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhum) who passed away before the final prohibition of intoxicants was revealed, affirming that they bore no sin for having consumed khamr during the period when it was still permissible.*"
3136,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:regarding Allah's saying: ""It may be that your Lord will raise you to a praised station (17:79)"" that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked about it and he said: ""It is the intercession"
3137,"Narrated Ibn Mas'ud:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered Makkah during the year of the Conquest"
3138,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by ʿAmr ibn ʿAlī Abū Ḥafṣ al-Fallās, who narrated from Abū ʿĀṣim, who narrated from ʿUthmān ibn Saʿd, who narrated from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him):**

A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, whenever I eat meat, I become aroused toward women, and my desire overtakes me, so I have forbidden meat upon myself.""

Thereupon, Allah, the Most High, revealed:

> *""O you who believe, do not forbid the good things which Allah has made lawful to you, and do not transgress. Indeed, Allah does not love the transgressors. And eat of what Allah has provided for you — lawful and good.""*
> (Sūrah al-Māʾidah, 5:87)

**[The narrator said:]** This is a *ḥasan gharīb* hadith.

Some of them narrated it from ʿUthmān ibn Saʿd in a *mursal* form, without mentioning Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him) in the chain. And Khālid al-Ḥadhdhāʾ narrated it from ʿIkrimah in a *mursal* form as well."
3139,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""The Quraish said to the Jews: 'Give us something that we can ask this man about.' So he said: 'Ask him about the Ruh.' So they asked him about the Ruh. So Allah Most High"
3140,"Narrated 'Abdullah:""I took a walk with the Prophet (ﷺ) on a farm in Al-Madinah"
3141,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""People will be gathered in three classes on the Day of Resurrection: A class walking"
3142,"Narrated Sa'eed ibn Ya'qoob al-Talaqani, who narrated from 'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak, who reported from 'Utbah ibn Abi Hakim, who narrated from 'Amr ibn Jariyah al-Lakhmi, from Abu Umayyah al-Sha'bani, who said:

""I came to Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani and said to him, 'How do you deal with this verse?' He asked, 'Which verse?' I said, 'His (Allah's) words: ""O you who believe, take care of your own selves. If you follow the right path, those who go astray cannot harm you.""' (5:105)

He replied: 'By Allah, you have indeed asked one who is well-informed about it. I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it, and he said: ""Rather, enjoin what is good and forbid what is evil. But when you see greed being obeyed, desires being followed, worldly matters being preferred, and every opinionated person impressed by their own opinion, then concern yourself with your own affairs and leave the common people. For indeed, ahead of you are days in which patience will be like holding onto burning coals. The one who acts rightfully during those days will have the reward of fifty men who perform deeds like yours.""'

'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak added: ""Someone other than 'Utbah informed me that it was asked: 'O Messenger of Allah, the reward of fifty men from among us or from among them?' He replied: 'No, rather the reward of fifty from among you.'""

Abu 'Eesa (al-Tirmidhi) said: ""This is a hasan gharib hadith."""
3143,"Narrated Safwan bin 'Assal Al-Muradi:""A Jew said to his companion: 'Accompany us to this Prophet.' So his companion said: 'Do not say: ""Prophet"
3144,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Sufyān ibn Wakīʿ** narrated to us: **Yaḥyā ibn Ādam** narrated to us, from **Ibn Abī Zāʾidah**, from **Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Qāsim**, from **ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Saʿīd**, from his father, from **Ibn ʿAbbāys** رضي الله عنهما, who said:

A man from Banū Sahm went out with Tamīm al-Dārī and ʿAdī ibn Badāʾ. The Sahmī man died in a land where there was no Muslim present. When the two companions returned with his estate, they (the heirs) found that a silver bowl inlaid with gold was missing. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ administered an oath to the two of them. Subsequently, the bowl was found in Makkah, and it was said: ""We purchased it from ʿAdī and Tamīm."" Then two men from among the heirs of the Sahmī stood and swore by Allah: ""Our testimony is more deserving than their testimony, and the bowl indeed belongs to their companion (the deceased).""

He (Ibn ʿAbbās) said: **""Concerning them was revealed:**

> *'O you who believe! Let there be witnesses between you...'*""** (Sūrat al-Māʾidah, 5:106)

This is a **ḥasan gharīb** hadith, and it is the hadith of Ibn Abī Zāʾidah."
3145,"Narrated Sa'eed bin Jubair:from Ibn 'Abbas regarding Allah's saying: ""And offer your Salat neither aloud nor in a low voice but follow a way between."" He said: ""It was revealed when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was hiding himself in Makkah"
3146,"Narrated Zirr bin Hubaish:""I said to Hudhaifah bin Al-Yaman: 'Did the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) perform Salat in Bait Al-Maqdis?' He said: 'No.' I said: 'But he did.' He said: 'You say that"
3147,"Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""I am the chief of the children of Adam on the Day of Judgement and I am not boasting"
3148,"Narrated Sa'eed bin Jubair:""I said to Ibn 'Abbas: 'Nawf Al-Bikali claims that Musa"
3149,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that Ubayy bin Ka'b narrated that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""The boy that Al-Khidr killed was destined to be a disbeliever the day he was created"
3150,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""He was called Al-Khadir because he sat on a barren Farwah and it turned green beneath him"
3151,"Narrated Abu Ad-Darda:that regarding Allah's saying: And there was under it a treasure belonging to them (18:82) - the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Gold and silver"
3152,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by Ahmad ibn Mani' (may Allah have mercy on him):**

Isḥāq ibn Yūsuf al-Azraq narrated to us, Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind narrated to us, from al-Shaʿbī, from Masrūq, who said:

""I was reclining in the company of ʿĀ'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), when she said: 'O Abū ʿĀ'ishah, there are three matters — whoever speaks of even one of them has indeed attributed a tremendous lie against Allah:

**First:** Whoever claims that Muḥammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saw his Lord has indeed attributed a tremendous lie against Allah, for Allah, the Most High, says:**

> *""Vision comprehends Him not, but He comprehends all vision. He is the Subtle, the All-Aware.""* (al-Anʿām, 6:103)

> *""It is not fitting for a man that Allah should speak to him except by revelation or from behind a veil.""* (al-Shūrā, 42:51)

Masrūq said: ""I was reclining, but I then sat up and said: 'O Umm al-Mu'minīn, grant me a moment and do not hasten me — does not Allah, the Most High, say:**

> *""And indeed he (Muḥammad) saw him (the angel) at a second descent.""* (al-Najm, 53:13)

> *""And indeed he saw him on the clear horizon.""* (al-Takwīr, 81:23)

She (ʿĀ'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her) said: 'By Allah, I was the first person to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about this matter.' He (peace and blessings be upon him) said:

**""That was only Jibrīl (peace be upon him). I did not see him in the form in which he was created except on these two occasions. I saw him descending from the heavens, his immense creation filling the space between the heavens and the earth.""**

**Second:** Whoever claims that Muḥammad (peace and blessings be upon him) concealed anything that Allah revealed to him has indeed attributed a tremendous lie against Allah, for Allah, the Most High, says:

> *""O Messenger, proclaim that which has been revealed to you from your Lord.""* (al-Mā'idah, 5:67)

**Third:** Whoever claims that he knows what tomorrow holds has indeed attributed a tremendous lie against Allah, for Allah, the Most High, says:

> *""Say: None in the heavens and the earth knows the unseen except Allah.""* (aml-Naml, 27:65)

---

**Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī, may Allah have mercy on him) said:** This is a *ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ* hadith. Masrūq ibn al-Ajdaʿ is known by the *kunyah* Abū ʿĀ'ishah, and he is Masrūq ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān — and thus was his name recorded in the official register (*dīwān*)."
3153,"Muḥammad ibn Mūsā al-Baṣrī al-Ḥarashī narrated to us, Ziyād ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Bakkāʾī narrated to us, ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib narrated from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said:

""Some people came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, shall we eat what we slaughter, but not eat what Allah causes to die?' So Allah, the Most High, revealed: 'So eat of that over which the name of Allah has been mentioned, if you are believers in His verses' (al-Anʿām: 118) until His statement: 'And if you obey them, indeed you would surely be polytheists' (al-Anʿām: 121).""

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: ""This is a ḥasan gharīb hadith. This hadith has also been narrated through other chains from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), and some of them narrated it from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in a mursal form."""
3154,"Narrated Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent me to Najran. They said to me: 'Do you people not recite: O sister of Harun (19:28) - while between Musa and 'Eisa there is such (gap) as there is?' I did not know how to respond to them. So when I returned to the Prophet (ﷺ)"
3155,"Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) recited: And warn them of a Day of griefs and regrets (19:39) and he said: 'Death will be brought as if it is a mixed black and white ram"
3156,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Abd ibn Humaid narrated to us:** Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Ghazwan, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said:

**""Three things, when they come to pass, no soul shall benefit from its faith if it had not believed before:** the Dajjal (the False Messiah), the Beast, and the rising of the sun from the west — or, from its place of setting.""

Abu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: **""This is a hasan sahih hadith.""**

Abu Hazim is al-Ashja'i al-Kufi, and his name is Salman, the freed slave of 'Azza al-Ashja'iyyah.

---

## Notes on the Translation

- **"""
3157,"Narrated Sa'eed bin Jubair:from Ibn 'Abbas who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to Jibra'il: 'What prevents you from visiting us more than you visit us?'"" He said: ""So this Ayah was revealed: And we descend not except by the command of your Lord. To Him belongs what is before us and what is behind us."" Up to the end of the Ayah (19:)"
3158,"Narrated As-Suddi:""I asked Murrah Al-Hamdani about the saying of Allah"
3159,"Narrated Shu'bah:from As-Suffi from Murrah: ""'Abdullah said: 'There is not one of you but will pass over it (19:71) - They pass over it"
3160,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""When Allah loves a slave He calls Jibra'il"
3161,"Narrated Masruq:""I heard Khabbab bin Al-Aratt saying: 'I came to Al-'As bin Wa'il As-Sahmi to collect a debt he owed me. He said: 'You shall not be given anything until you deny Muhammad.' So I said: 'No"
3162,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:""While the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was returning from Khaibar he traveled during the night until he became sleepy and he sat down to rest. Then he said: 'O Bilal! Stand guard for us for the night.'"" He said: 'So Bilal performed Salat"
3163,"Narrated Abu Sa'eed:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Woe is the valley of Jahannam"
3164,"Narrated 'Aishah:that a man came and sat in front of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I have two slaves who lie to me"
3165,
3166,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) stood to deliver a Khutbah"
3167,"Narrated 'Imran bin Husain:when (the following) was revealed: ""O mankind! Have Taqwa of your Lord! Verily the earthquake of the hour is a terrible thing..."" up to His saying: ""But Allah's torment is severe...(22:1 & 2)"" - he said: ""These Ayat were revealed while he (ﷺ) was on a journey and he said: 'Do you know what Day this is?' So they said: 'Allah and His Messenger know better.' He said: 'That is the day when Allah says to Adam: Send forth those who are to be sent to the Fire. So he says: O Lord! How many are to be sent? He says: Nine-hundred and ninety-nine in the Fire"
3168,"Narrated 'Imran bin Husain:""We were with the Prophet (ﷺ) on a journey when some of his Companions fell behind. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) raised his voice reciting these two Ayat: ""O mankind! Have Taqwa of your Lord! Verily the earthquake of the hour is a terrible thing..."" up to His saying: but Allah's torment is severe (21:1 & 2)."" When his Companions heard that"
3169,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin Az-Zubair:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""It is only called Al-Bait Al-'Atiq because it has not been conquered by a tyrant"
3170,
3171,"Narrated Sa'eed bin Jubair:""When the Prophet (ﷺ) was expelled from Makkah a man said: 'They have driven out their Prophet' so (the following) was revealed: ""Permission (to fight) is given to those who are fought against"
3172,"Narrated 'Umar bin Al-Khattab [may Allah be pleased with him]:""When revelation came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
3173,Narrated Anas bin Malik:that Ar-Rubai' bint An-Nadr came to the Prophet (ﷺ) - and her son Harithah bin Suraqah had been killed on the Day of Badr
3174,"Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin [Sa'eed bin] Wahb - that is Al-Hamdani:that 'Aishah the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""I asked about the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about this Ayah: And those who give that which they give with their hearts full of fear... (23:60)"" 'Aishah said: ""Are they those who drink Khamr and steal?"" He said: ""No"
3175,"Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Therein they will grin"
3176,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by Ibn Abi 'Umar, who narrated from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Zaid bin Yuthay', who said:**

""We asked 'Alī (may Allāh be pleased with him): 'With what were you sent during the [Farewell] Hajj?' He replied: 'I was sent with four [commands]: That no one should circumambulate the House [i.e., the Ka'bah] in a state of nakedness; that whoever has a covenant between himself and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), it shall remain until its [stipulated] duration; and whoever has no covenant, then his term shall be four months; and no soul shall enter Paradise except a believing soul; and the polytheists and the Muslims shall not gather [for pilgrimage] after this year of theirs.'""

Abū 'Īsā [al-Tirmidhī] said: ""This is a *ḥasan* (good) hadith, and it is the hadith of Sufyān bin 'Uyaynah from Abū Ishaq. And it was narrated by al-Thawrī from Abū Ishaq from some of his companions from 'Alī. And in this chapter [there are narrations] from Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him).""

**Narrated by Naṣr bin 'Alī and others, who said:** Sufyān bin 'Uyaynah narrated to us from Abū Ishaq, from Zaid bin Yuthay', from 'Alī, a similar narration.

**Narrated by 'Alī bin Khashram, who narrated:** Sufyān bin 'Uyaynah narrated to us from Abū Ishaq, from Zaid bin Uthay', from 'Alī, a similar narration.

Abū 'Īsā [al-Tirmidhī] said: ""It has been narrated from Ibn 'Uyaynah both versions — it is said 'from Ibn Uthay'' and 'from Ibn Yuthay'' — and the correct one is **Zaid bin Uthay'**. Shu'bah narrated from Abū Ishaq from Zaid other than this hadith, and he erred in it, saying 'Zaid bin Uthayl,' and he is not followed [in that error]. And in this chapter [there are narrations] from Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him).""

---

*Peace and blessings be upon our Prophet Muḥammad, his family, and all his Companions.*"
3177,"Narrated Sa'eed bin Jubair:""I was asked about those who were involved in the case of Li'an and if they are to be separated"
3178,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""Hilal bin Umayyah went to the Prophet (ﷺ) and accused his wife of committing illegal sexual intercourse with Sharik bin Sahma. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Either you produce proof"
3179,"# Translation of the Hadith

Al-Ḥusayn ibn Yazīd al-Kūfī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Ḥarb narrated to us, from Ghutayf ibn Aʿyan, from Muṣʿab ibn Saʿd, from ʿAdī ibn Ḥātim, who said:

""I came to the Prophet ﷺ while I was wearing a gold cross around my neck. He ﷺ said: **'O ʿAdī, cast away this idol (wathan) from yourself.'** And I heard him ﷺ reciting from Sūrah Barāʾah (al-Tawbah): *'They have taken their scholars and monks as lords besides Allāh.'* He ﷺ said: **'Verily, they did not used to worship them; however, when they (the scholars and monks) declared something lawful for them, they would deem it lawful, and when they declared something unlawful for them, they would deem it unlawful.'**""

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: ""This is a *gharīb* (uncommon) hadith. We do not know it except through the narration of ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Ḥarb. And Ghutayf ibn Aʿyan is not well-known (*maʿrūf*) in the science of hadith.""

---

**Note:** This narration is recorded in *Sunan al-Tirmidhī* and is classified as *gharīb* due to the weakness of Ghutayf ibn Aʿyan in the chain of transmission. The hadith illustrates the gravity of blind following (*taqlīd*) of religious authorities in declaring lawful and unlawful matters without divine authority, which constitutes a form of *shirk* in legislation (*tashrīʿ*)."
3180,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by Ziyād ibn Ayyūb al-Baghdādī, who narrated from ʿAffān ibn Muslim, who narrated from Hammām, who narrated from Thābit, from Anas رضي الله عنه, that Abū Bakr رضي الله عنه related to him, saying:**

""I said to the Prophet ﷺ while we were in the cave: 'If any one of them were to look at his feet, he would surely see us beneath his feet.'""

**The Prophet ﷺ then said:**

**""O Abū Bakr! What is your opinion of two, the Third of them being Allāh?""**

---

**Commentary by the Compiler:**

This is a *ḥasan ṣaḥīh gharīb* (good, sound, and singular) hadith. It is known only from the narration of Hammām, who is its sole narrator in this chain. However, this hadith has also been narrated by Ḥibbān ibn Hilāl and others from Hammām in a similar fashion.

---

*This narration is famously known as the Hadith of the Cave (Hadith al-Ghār), referring to the event of the Hijrah when the Prophet ﷺ and Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq رضي الله"
3181,"Narrated 'Abdullah:""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! What is the worst sin?' He said: 'That you make and equal to Allah"
3182,"Narrated 'Abdullah:""I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) which sin is the worst.' He said: 'That you make an equal to Allah while it is He who created you"
3183,"Narrated 'Aishah:""When this Ayah was revealed: 'And warn your tribe of near kindred (26:214).' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'O Safiyyah bint 'Abdul-Muttalib! O Fatimah bint Muhammad! O Banu 'Abdul-Muttalib! I have no power to help you at all before Allah! Ask of me whatever you want from my wealth"
3184,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:""When (the following) was revealed: 'And warn your tribe of near kindred (26:214)' the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gathered the (families) of the Quraish (calling them) one and all"
3185,"Narrated Qasamah bin Zuhair:""Al-Ash'ari said: 'When (the following) was revealed: 'And warn your tribe of near kindred (26:214)' the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) placed his fingers in his ears"
3186,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""A beast will emerge from the earth. With it shall be the ring of Sulaiman and the staff of Musa. It will brighten the face of the believer"
3187,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us** — **Abd ar-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us** — **Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us**, from **az-Zuhri**, from **Ubayd ibn as-Sabbak**, that **Zayd ibn Thabit** — رضي الله عنه — narrated to him, saying:

Abu Bakr as-Siddiq — رضي الله عنه — sent for me at the time of the massacre of the people of Yamamah, and behold, Umar ibn al-Khattab — رضي الله عنه — was with him. Abu Bakr said: ""Indeed, Umar ibn al-Khattab has come to me and said: 'Verily, slaughter has raged fiercely among the reciters of the Qur'an on the day of Yamamah, and I fear that slaughter may rage among the reciters in all the battlefields, and thus much of the Qur'an will be lost. I am of the opinion that you should command the collection of the Qur'an.'""

Abu Bakr said to Umar: ""How can I do something that the Messenger of Allah — صلى الله عليه وسلم — did not do?"" Umar said: ""By Allah, it is goodness."" He continued to press me on the matter until Allah expanded my chest for that for which He had expanded the chest of Umar, and I came to see in it what he had seen.

Zayd said: Abu Bakr said: ""You are a young, intelligent man, and we do not suspect you. You used to write down the Revelation for the Messenger of Allah — صلى الله عليه وسلم — so pursue and collect the Qur'an.""

Zayd said: ""By Allah, had they tasked me with moving a mountain from among the mountains, it would not have been heavier upon me than this task."" I said: ""How can you do something that the Messenger of Allah — صلى الله عليه وسلم — did not do?"" Abu Bakr said: ""By Allah, it is goodness."" Abu Bakr and Umar continued to press me on the matter until Allah expanded my chest for that for which He had expanded the chests of Abu Bakr and Umar.

So I pursued the Qur'an, collecting it from **riga'** (scraps of leather), **'usub** (palm stalks), **likhaf** (thin stones), and the breasts of men. I found the last verses of Surah Bara'ah (at-Tawbah) with **Khuzaymah ibn Thabit** — رضي الله"
3188,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Anas, that Ḥudhayfah came to ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān — may Allah be pleased with them both — while he was engaged in military campaigns alongside the people of Shām in the conquest of Armenia and Adharbījān together with the people of ʿIrāq. Ḥudhayfah observed their differences regarding the Qurʾān, so he said to ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, ""O Commander of the Faithful, take hold of this Ummah before they differ concerning the Book as the Jews and the Christians differed.""**

**So ʿUthmān sent to Ḥafṣah — may Allah be pleased with her — saying, ""Send us the written sheets (al-ṣuḥuf) so that we may copy them into codices (maṣāḥif), and then we shall return them to you."" Ḥafṣah sent the sheets to ʿUthmān, and ʿUthmān dispatched word to Zayd ibn Thābit, Saʿid ibn al-ʿĀṣ, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām, and ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr — may Allah be pleased with them — saying, ""Copy the sheets into codices."" And he said to the three Qurayshite men, ""Whenever you and Zayd ibn Thābit differ concerning anything, write it in the dialect of Quraysh, for indeed the Qurʾān was revealed in their tongue.""**

**Until they had copied the sheets into codices, ʿUthmān sent to every region a codex from those codices they had copied.**

**Al-Zuhrī said: Khārijah ibn Zayd ibn Thābit narrated to me that Zayd ibn Thābit — may Allah be pleased with him — said: ""I lost a verse from Sūrat al-Aḥzāb which I used to hear the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, recite:**

**'Among the believers are men who have been true to their covenant with Allah; among them are those who have fulfilled their vow…' (al-Aḥzāb 33:23)**

**So I searched for it and found it with Khuzaymah ibn Thābit — or Abū Khuzaymah — and I appended it to its sūrah.""**

**Al-Zuhrī said: ""They differed that day concerning *al-Tābūt* and *al-Tābūh*. The Qurayshites said *al-Tābūt*, while Zayd said *al-Tābūh*. Their difference was raised to ʿUthmān, and he said, 'Write it as *al-Tābūt*, for indeed it was revealed in the tongue of Quraysh.'""**

**Al-Zuhrī said: ""ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUtbah informed me that ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd — may Allah be pleased with him — disliked Zayd ibn Thābit's copying of the codices and said, 'O company of Muslims! I am being removed from the transcription of the Muṣḥaf while it is being undertaken by a man — and by Allah, I embraced Islam while he was yet in the loins of a disbeliever' — meaning Zayd ibn Thābit. And for that reason ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd said, 'O people of ʿIrāq, conceal the codices that are with you and keep them hidden, for indeed Allah says: *""And whoever acts dishonestly shall bring forth his dishonesty on the Day of Resurrection""* (Āl ʿImrān 3:161). So meet Allah with the codices.'""**

**Al-Zuhrī said: ""It has reached me that this statement of Ibn Masʿūd was disliked by men among the eminent Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him.""**

**[The compiler said:] This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith. It is the hadith of al-Zuhrī; we do not know it except from his narration.**"
3189,"Narrated Umm Hani:that regarding Allah's saying: '...And you practice evil in your meetings... (29:29) that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""They would throw pebbles at people of the land and make a mockery of them"
3190,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that regarding ""Alif Lam Mim. The Romans have been defeated"" (In the nearest land"
3191,"Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Minhal narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said:

""When Allah drowned Pharaoh, Pharaoh said: 'I believe that there is no god but the One in whom the Children of Israel believe.' Jibril (peace be upon him) then said: 'O Muhammad, if you could have seen me taking mud from the sea and stuffing it into his mouth, out of fear that mercy might reach him.'""

Abu Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: ""This is a hasan (good) hadith."""
3192,"Narrated by Muhammad ibn ʿAbd al-Aʿlā al-Ṣanʿānī, who narrated from Khālid ibn al-Ḥārith, who reported from Shuʿbah, who informed me from ʿAdīy ibn Thābit and ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās — one of them mentioned that the Prophet ﷺ said:

""Indeed, Jibrīl (peace be upon him) used to thrust clay into the mouth of Firʿawn, lest he should say *Lā ilāha illā Allāh* (There is no god but Allah), and thus Allah would have mercy on him — or, lest Allah should have mercy on him.""

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: *This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ gharīb hadith from this chain of narration.*"
3193,"Narrated Niyar bin Mukram Al-Aslami:""When (the following) was revealed: 'Alif Lam Mim. The Romans have been defeated. In the nearest land"
3194,"Narrated Abu Umamah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Do not sell the female singers"
3195,"Anas bin Malik said about this Ayah:Their sides forsake their beds (32:16) - ""It was revealed about waiting for [this] Salat which you call Al-'Atamah"
3196,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Allah Most High said: 'I have prepared for My righteous worshipers what no eye has seen"
3197,"Abd ibn Humaid narrated to us, from Husayn al-Ju'fi, from Zāʾidah, from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr, from ʿAbd ar-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from Muʿādh ibn Jabal, who said:

A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, and said: ""O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about a man who met a woman with whom he had no prior acquaintance, and he did to her everything that a man might do with his wife, except that he did not actually consummate the act?""

At that moment, Allah, Exalted is He, revealed: *""Establish prayer at the two ends of the day and in the early hours of the night. Indeed, good deeds remove evil deeds. That is a reminder for those who remember.""* (Hūd 11:114)

The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, then commanded the man to perform ablution and pray.

Muʿādh said: I asked, ""O Messenger of Allah, is this ruling specific to this man, or does it apply to all believers in general?""

He replied: **""Rather, it applies to all believers in general.""**

Abū ʿĪsā [at-Tirmidhī] said: This hadith is not connected (*muttaṣil*) in its chain of narration, for ʿAbd ar-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā did not hear directly from Muʿādh. Muʿādh ibn Jabal passed away during the caliphate of ʿUmar, and when ʿUmar was martyred, ʿAbd ar-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā was only a young boy of six years of age. He did, however, narrate from ʿUmar and saw him.

Furthermore, Shuʿbah narrated this same hadith from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr, from ʿAbd ar-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, as a *mursal* (disconnected) narration."
3198,"# Hadith of Ibn Mas'ūd (may Allāh be pleased with him) Regarding the Expiation for an Unlawful Kiss

**Narration Chain:**
Muhammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Sa'īd narrated to us — from Sulaymān al-Taymī — from Abū 'Uthmān — from Ibn Mas'ūd (may Allāh be pleased with him):

## Text:

That a man committed an unlawful kiss with a woman, and so he came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him regarding its expiation. Thereupon the following verse was revealed:

> *""Establish prayer at the two ends of the day and in the approaching hours of the night. Indeed, good deeds remove evil deeds. That is a reminder for those mindful.""*
> — [Sūrah Hūd 11:114]

The man asked, **""Is this for me alone, O Messenger of Allāh ﷺ?""**

The Prophet ﷺ replied: **""It is for you and for anyone who acts upon it from my Ummah.""**

## Authentication:

Abū 'Īsā (al-Tirmidhī, raḥimahullāh) said: **""This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith.""**

---

*Ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam.*"
3199,"Narrated Anas:""My paternal uncle Anas bin An-Nadr - after whom I was named - did not participate in the battle of Badr with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). This distressed him and he said: 'I was absent from the first battle which the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) attended. By Allah! If Allah gives me the opportunity to participate in another battle along with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
3200,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:""My paternal uncle was absent from the fighting of Badr"
3201,"Narrated Musa bin Talhah:""I entered upon Mu'awiyah and he said:' Shall I not give you some good news?' I said: 'Of course!' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: 'Talhah is among those who fulfilled their vow"
3202,"# Hadith Translation

**Narrated by Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him):**

Maḥmūd ibn Khidāsh al-Baghdādī narrated to us, saying: Saif ibn Muḥammad al-Thawrī narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ regarding Allāh's statement:

> **""And We have made some of these [fruits] superior to others in taste""** (Sūrat al-Raʿd, 13:4)

The Prophet ﷺ said: **""The inferior date (al-daql), the Persian [date], the sweet, and the sour.""**

He (the compiler) said: **""This is a ḥasan gharīb hadith. It was also narrated by Zayd ibn Abī Unaysah from al-Aʿmash in a similar manner. Saif ibn Muḥammad is the brother of ʿAmmār ibn Muḥammad, and ʿAmmār is more reliable (athbat) than him. He is the son of the maternal aunt of Sufyān al-Thawrī.""**

---

*Note: The hadith explains the Qur'ānic verse regarding the variation in the quality and taste of fruits, illustrating that even among the same category of produce, there exists a hierarchy of excellence — from the low-quality date (daql) to the finest varieties, and from the sweet to the sour — all by the decree and wisdom of Allāh, the Most High.*"
3203,"Narrated 'Aishah [may Allah be pleased with her]:""When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was ordered to tell his wives to make a choice"
3204,"Narrated 'Umar bin Abi Salamah - the step-son of the Prophet (ﷺ):""When these Ayat were revealed to the Prophet (ﷺ): 'Allah only wishes to remove the Rijs from you"
3205,"Narrated to us Ibn Abi 'Umar, narrated to us Sufyan, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, who said:

'Ā'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, recited this verse: *""On the Day when the earth will be changed to another earth""* (Sūrah Ibrāhīm, 14:48). She said: ""O Messenger of Allah, where will the people be?"" He, peace and blessings be upon him, replied: **""Upon the Ṣirāṭ (the Bridge over Hellfire).""**

This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith. It has also been narrated through other chains from 'Ā'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her."
3206,"Narrated 'Aishah [may Allah be pleased with her]:""If the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was to have concealed anything that was revealed to him"
3207,"Narrated 'Aishah [may Allah be pleased with her]:""If the Prophet (ﷺ) was to have hidden anything from the Revelation"
