3283,"Narrated 'Ata:from Ibn 'Abbas (regarding this Ayah): Those who avoid great sins and Al-Fawahish except Al-Lamam (minor sins) (53:32). He said: ""The Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'Your forgiveness"
3284,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by Anas (may Allah be pleased with him):**

My uncle, Anas ibn An-Nadr — after whom I was named — had not been present at the Battle of Badr alongside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and this weighed heavily upon him. He said:

*""The first battle in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) participated, and I was absent from it — nay, by Allah! If Allah grants me to witness another engagement alongside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), Allah shall surely see what I shall do.""*

He feared to say anything more than that. He then joined the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) at the Battle of Uhud the following year. Sa'd ibn Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) encountered him and said:

*""O Abu 'Amr, where are you going?""*

He replied:

*""Ah, I smell the fragrance of Paradise — I find it wafting from beyond Uhud!""*

He fought until he was martyred. Upon his body were found eighty-some wounds — between sword strikes, spear thrusts, and arrow shots. My aunt, Ar-Rubayyi' bint An-Nadr (may Allah be pleased with her), said:

*""I could not recognize my brother except by his fingertips.""*

And concerning him, the following verse was revealed:

> **""Among the believers are men who have been true to their covenant with Allah. Among them are those who have fulfilled their vow [to the death], and among them are those who are [still] waiting, and they have not changed [their commitment] in the least.""**
> *(Al-Ahzab, 33:23)*

Abu 'Isa (at-Tirmidhi, may Allah have mercy on him) said: **""This is a hasan sahih hadith.""**

---

*Peace and blessings be upon our Prophet Muhammad, his family, and his Companions.*"
