Abu Hafs 'Amr ibn al-Fallas narrated to us: Abu Qutaybah Salam ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Suhayl ibn Abi Hazm al-Qata'i narrated to us: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) recited: *""Indeed, those who have said, 'Our Lord are Allah,' and then remained steadfast""* (Qur'an 41:30), and he (peace be upon him) said: ""The people have said it, then most of them disbelieved after that. So whoever dies upon this [declaration] is among those who remained steadfast.""

Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: This is a *gharib* hadith; we do not know it except through this chain. I heard Abu Zur'ah saying that 'Affan narrated a hadith from 'Amr ibn 'Ali, and there are narrations regarding the meaning of *'they remained steadfast'* in this verse from the Prophet (peace be upon him), Abu Bakr, and 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both)."
