3342,"# Hadith Translation

**Narrated by 'Alqamah (may Allah be pleased with him):**

I said to Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), ""Did anyone among you accompany the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) on the Night of the Jinn?"" He replied, ""None of us accompanied him. However, we missed him one night in Makkah, and we said, 'He has been seized or taken away — what has happened to him!' So we spent the worst night that any people ever spent. When morning came, or as the light of dawn appeared, suddenly we saw him coming from the direction of Hira'. He said: So they mentioned to him what they had been going through. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: **'The caller of the Jinn came to me, so I went to them and recited (the Qur'an) to them.'** Then he set off and showed us their traces and the traces of their fires.

Al-Sha'bi said: They asked him for provisions, and they were from the Jinn of Al-Jazirah. So he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: **'Every bone over which the name of Allah has not been mentioned will come to you with the most abundant meat upon it, and every dung pellet or dropping is fodder for your animals.'**

Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: **'So do not use them (bones and droppings) for istinja (cleaning after relieving yourselves), for they are the provisions of your brothers among the Jinn.'**

Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: This is a **hasan sahih** (good and authentic) hadith."
