3352,"Narrated to us was ʿAbdullāh ibn Isḥāq al-Jawharī al-Baṣrī, who narrated to us from Abū Zayd, from Shuʿbah, from Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind, who said: I heard al-Shaʿbī narrating from Abū Jābirah ibn al-Ḍaḥḥāk, who said: ""A man among us would have two or three names, and he would be called by one of them, and perhaps he would dislike it. So this verse was revealed: **'And do not call one another by [offensive] nicknames'** (al-Ḥujurāt, 49:11).""

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith.

Abū Jābirah is the brother of Thābit ibn al-Ḥaḥḥāk ibn Khalīfah, an Anṣārī. Abū Zayd is Saʿīd ibn al-Rabīʿ, the companion of al-Harawī, a trustworthy (thiqah) Baṣrī narrator.

Narrated to us was Abū Salamah, Yaḥyā ibn Khalaf, who narrated to us from Bishr ibn al-Mufaḍḍal, from Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind, from al-Shaʿbī, from Abū Jābirah ibn al-Ḍaḥḥāk, with a similar narration.

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith."
