3358,"Abd ibn Humaid narrated to us: Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us: Salam ibn Sulayman al-Nahwi, Abu al-Mundhir, narrated to us: Asim ibn Abi al-Najud narrated from Abu Wa'il, from al-Harith ibn Yazid al-Bakri, who said:

""I arrived in Madinah and entered the mosque, and lo, it was crowded with people. Black banners were fluttering, and Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) stood before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) with a sword girded at his side. I asked, 'What is the matter with the people?' They said, 'He intends to dispatch Amr ibn al-As on an expedition.'""

He then narrated the hadith in its entirety, similar in meaning to the hadith of Sufyan ibn Uyaynah.

It is also said that he is known as al-Harith ibn Hassan as well."
