3406,Ar-Irbad bin Sariyah (ra) narrated that:The Prophet (ﷺ) would not sleep until he had recited Al-Musabbihat
3407,A man from Banu Hanzalah said:“I accompanied Shaddad bin Aws [may Allah be pleased with him] on a journey
3408,Ali [may Allah be pleased with him] said:“Fatimah complained to me about her hands blistering from grinding flour. So I said: ‘If you were to approach your father and ask him for a servant?’ So he (the Prophet) said: ‘Should I not direct the two of you
3409,Ali [may Allah be pleased with him] said:“Fatimah went to the Prophet complaining of her hands blistering
3410,Abdullah bin `Amr [may Allah be pleased with both of them] said:“The Messenger of Allah said: ‘There are two characteristics over which a Muslim man does not guard
3411,Abdullah bin Amr [may Allah be pleased with him] said:“I saw the Messenger of Allah counting At-Tasbīḥ.”
3412,Ka’b bin Ujrah narrated that:The Prophet said: “There are Mu’aqqibat
3413,Zaid bin Thabit (ra) said:“We were ordered to say the Tasbīḥ at the end of every Salat thirty-three times
3414,"# Hadith of the Stations of Paradise's Inhabitants

**Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us** — Shabābah informed us, from Isrā'īl, from Thuwayr, who said: **I heard Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with both of them) saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:**

> *""Indeed, the lowest-ranking person among the inhabitants of Paradise in station shall be the one who looks upon his gardens, his spouses, his servants, and his couches as far as a journey of a thousand years. And the most honoured of them in the sight of Allah shall be the one who gazes upon His Face morning and evening.""*

**Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited:**

> *""Faces, that Day, shall be radiant, looking toward their Lord.""* (Qiyāmah, 75:22–23)

**Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said:** This is a *gharīb* (uncommon/singular) hadith. More than one narrator has transmitted it from Isrā'īl in this form, as a *marfūʾ* (elevated) narration. ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abjar narrated it from Thuwayr, from Ibn ʿUmar, as his own statement (*mawqūf*), without elevating it. And al-Ashjaʿī narrated it from Sufyān, from Thuwayr, from Mujāhid, from Ibn ʿUmar, as his own statement, without elevating it. And we do not know of anyone who mentioned Mujāhid in this chain other than al-Thawrī.

**Abū Kurayb narrated that to us** — ʿUbayd Allāh al-Ashjaʿī narrated to us, from Sufyān.

**Thuwayr** is known by the *kunyah* of Abū Jahm. **Abū Fākhitah** is his name: Saʿīd ibn ʿIlāqah.

---

*Transmitted by Imām Abū ʿĪsā Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī (may Allah have mercy upon him) in his Jāmiʿ.*"
3415,Maslamah bin `Amr said:“`Umair bin Hani used to perform a thousand prostrations every day and recite a hundred thousand Tasbīḥs every day.”
3416,Rabi`ah bin Ka`b Al-Aslami said:“I used to spend the night at the door of the Prophet (ﷺ)
