3449,"# Translation of the Hadith

Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Abu Ja'far ar-Razi, from ar-Rabi', from Abu al-Aliyah, that the Prophet ﷺ mentioned their gods, and they said: ""Describe your Lord for us."" He said: Then Jibril (عليه السلام) came to him with this Surah: **""Say: He is Allah, the One""** (Surah al-Ikhlas). He then mentioned something similar to it, and he did not mention in it a chain from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, and this is more authentic (aṣaḥḥ) than the hadith of Abu Sa'd. And Abu Sa'd's name is Muhammad ibn Maysar, and Abu Ja'far ar-Razi's name is Isa, and Abu al-Aliyah's name is Rufay', and he was a slave whom a Sabian woman had manumitted."
