3483,"Abū Kurayb narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr — he is the Salūlī — informed us, from Ibrāhīm ibn Yūsuf ibn Abī Isḥāq, from his father, from Abū Isḥāq, from Abū Burdah, from al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib, may Allāh be pleased with them both, who said:

""The Messenger of Allāh, peace and blessings be upon him, would rest upon his right side when sleeping, and then he would say:

**'My Lord, protect me from Your punishment on the day You resurrect Your servants.'**

Abū ʿĪsā said: This is a *ḥasan gharīb* hadith from this chain. Ath-Thawrī narrated this hadith from Abū Isḥāq from al-Barāʾ, without mentioning anyone between them. Shuʿbah narrated from Abū Isḥāq from Abū ʿUbaydah and another man from al-Barāʾ. And Isrāʾīl narrated from Abū Isḥāq from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd from al-Barāʾ, and from Abū Isḥāq from Abū ʿUbaydah from ʿAbdullāh from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, a similar narration."""
3484,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Abdullāh ibn 'Abd al-Rahmān narrated to us, 'Amr ibn 'Awn informed us, Khālid ibn 'Abdullāh informed us from Suhayl, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said:**

The Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) used to command us, when one of us took his bed, to say:

*""O Allāh, Lord of the heavens, Lord of the earths, our Lord, and Lord of everything; Splitter of the seed and the stone, and Sender down of the Tawrāh, the Injīl, and the Qur'ān — I seek refuge in You from the evil of every possessor of evil, You hold him by his forelock. You are the First, so nothing is before You; You are the Last, so nothing is after You; the Manifest (al-Ẓāhir), so nothing is above You; and the Hidden (al-Bāṭin), so nothing is beyond You. Settle my debt for me and enrich me from poverty.""*

Abū 'Īsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: **This is a hasan sahīh hadith.**"
