3504,"Narrated by Yahya ibn Musa and others, who said: 'Umar ibn Yunus informed us, who said: 'Ikrimah ibn 'Ammar narrated to us, who said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, who said: Abu Salamah narrated to us, who said:

""I asked 'Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her): 'With what did the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) begin his prayer when he stood up at night?' She replied: 'When he stood up at night, he would begin his prayer by saying:

""O Allah, Lord of Jibril, Mika'il, and Israfil, Creator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the seen, You judge between Your servants in that wherein they differ. Guide me to the truth in that wherein they differ, by Your permission. Indeed, You guide whom You will to the Straight Path.""'

He (the narrator) said: 'This is a hasan gharib hadith.'"""
