3623,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Qutaybah narrated to us; al-Layth narrated to us, from Muḥammad ibn Qayṣ, the storyteller of ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, from Abū Ṣirmah, from Abū Ayyūb, that he said when death approached him:**

*""I had concealed from you something I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say:*

**'Were it not that you commit sins, Allah would have created a creation who would commit sins, and He would forgive them.'**""

He (the narrator) said: **""This is a ḥasan gharīb hadith.""**

It has also been narrated from Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb, from Abū Ayyūb, from the Prophet ﷺ, with a similar meaning.

**Qutaybah narrated that to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Rijāl narrated to us, from ʿUmar, the freedman of Ghafrā, from Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb, from Abū Ayyūb, from the Prophet ﷺ, with a similar meaning.**

---

*This hadith is classified as ḥasan gharīb (good and singular in its chain). It highlights the profound mercy of Allah, Most High, and the wisdom behind the existence of sin and repentance among His creation.*"
3624,"Narrated Abu Al-'Ala:from Samurah bin Jundab that he said: ""We were with the Prophet (ﷺ) and we would take turns (eating) from a bowl from the morning till the evening. Ten would stand and ten would sit."" We said: ""So what was filling it up?' He said: ""What are you amazed at? It wasn't filled up from anywhere but here"
3625,"Narrated 'Ali bin Abi Talib:""I was with the Prophet (ﷺ) in Makkah. We departed to one of its suburbs"
3626,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to give Khutbah next to a tree"
3627,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: 'How shall I know that you are a Prophet?' He said: 'If I were to call this date cluster from this palm tree"
3628,"Narrated Abu Zaid bin Akhtab:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) wiped his hand over my face and supplicated for me."" 'Azrah (one of the narrators) said: ""Indeed he lived for one-hundred and twenty years"
3629,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:""Abu Talhah said to Umm Sulaim: 'I heard the voice of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sounding weak and I sensed some hunger in it. Do you have anything? She said: 'Yes.' So she got some loaves of wheat bread"
3630,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:""I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) at the time when the 'Asr prayer had drawn near"
3631,"Narrated 'Aishah:""The first of what the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) initiated with of Prophethood"
3632,"Narrated by al-Hasan ibn 'Arafah, narrated by Yazid ibn Harun, from 'Abd ar-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr al-Qurashi al-Mulaiki, from Musa ibn 'Uqba, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever among you has the door of supplication opened for him, the doors of mercy are opened for him. And nothing is asked of Allah—meaning nothing is more beloved to Him—than that He be asked for well-being (al-'afiyah).""

And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Indeed, supplication benefits against what has descended and what has not yet descended. So upon you, O servants of Allah, is supplication.""

It is said: This is a *gharib* (uncommon) hadith. We do not know it except through the narration of 'Abd ar-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr al-Qurashi, who is the Makkan al-Mulaiki, and he is considered weak (*da'if*) in hadith; some of the scholars of knowledge deemed him weak on account of his memory.

And Isra'il narrated this hadith from 'Abd ar-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, from Musa ibn 'Uqba, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: ""Nothing is asked of Allah that is more beloved to Him than well-being (al-'afiyah)."""
3633,Narrated 'Aishah:that Al-Harith bin Hisham asked the Prophet (ﷺ): 'How does the Revelation come to you?' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Sometimes it comes to me like the ringing of a bell and that is the hardest upon me
3634,"Narrated Al-Bara:""I have not seen anyone with hair past his shoulders in a red Hullah more handsome than the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He had hair that would flow on his shoulders"
3635,"Narrated Abu Ishaq:""A man asked Al-Bara: 'Was the face of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) like a sword?' He said: 'No"
3636,"Narrated Abu Ishaq:""A man asked Al-Bara: 'Was the face of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) like a sword?' He said: 'No, like the moon.'"""
3637,"Narrated to us Mūsā ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Kindī al-Kūfī, narrated to us Zayd ibn Ḥabbāb, and Sufyān al-Thawrī informed me from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from al-Shaʿbī, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Laylā, from Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣarī, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said:

""Whoever says ten times: 'There is no deity except Allah alone, without partner; to Him belongs sovereignty and to Him belongs praise; He gives life and causes death, and He is over all things competent' — it will be for him equivalent to freeing four slaves from the descendants of Ismāʿīl.""

It is also narrated that this hadith was reported from Abū Ayyūb as a mawqūf (a statement attributed to the Companion rather than the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him)."
3638,"Narrated 'Urwah:that 'Aishah said: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not speak quickly like you do now"
3639,Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would repeat a statement three times so that it could be understood
3640,"Narrated Ibn Jaz:""I have not seen anyone who smiled more than the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
