3652,Narrated Jabir [bin 'Abdullah]:that he heard Mu'awiyah bin Abi Sufyan giving a Khutbah
3653,"Narrated 'Aishah [may Allah be pleased with her]:""The Prophet (ﷺ) died when he was sixty-three years old"
3654,
3655,"# Hadith Translation

**Narrated to us** Bushr ibn Mu'adh al-'Aqadi al-Basri: **Narrated to us** Hammad ibn Waqid, from Isra'il, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from 'Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: **The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:**

**""Ask Allah from His bounty, for indeed, Allah, the Almighty and Glorified, loves to be asked, and the best form of worship is the anticipation of relief.""**

**Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said:** Thus did Hammad ibn Waqid narrate this hadith, though he was **contradicted** in his narration. This Hammad ibn Waqid is al-Saffar; he is **not a hafiz** (strong memorizer), and he is, in our estimation, a Basri shaykh. **Abu Nu'aym** also narrated this hadith from Isra'il, from Hakim ibn Jubayr, from a man, from the Prophet ﷺ, as a **mursal** (disconnected) narration. And the hadith of Abu Nu'aym is **more likely to be the more authentic** (ahaqq/sahih) of the two.

---

### Scholarly Notes:

- **""Ask Allah from His bounty""** (سَلُوا اللَّهَ مِنْ فَضْلِهِ): This refers to supplicating to Allah and requesting from His abundant generosity, indicating the virtue of **du'ā** (supplication).

- **""The best form of worship is the anticipation of relief""** (وَأَفْضَلُ الْعِبَادَةِ انْتِظَارُ الْفَرَجِ): This signifies that among the highest acts of worship is maintaining hope and patient expectation that relief (faraj) from Allah will come, especially during times of hardship.

- **Mursal** ("
3656,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin Shaqiq:""I said to 'Aishah: 'Which of the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) were the most beloved to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?' She said: 'Abu Bakr.' I said: 'Then who?' She said: ''Umar.' I said: ""Then who?' She said: 'Then Abu 'Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah.'"" He said: ""I said: 'Then who?''"" He said: ""Then she was silent"
3657,"Narrated Abu Sa'eed:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed the people of the higher levels"
3658,"Narrated Ibn Abi Mu'alla:from his father: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave a Khutbah one day and said: 'Indeed there is a man whose Lord has given him the choice between living in this life as long as he wishes to live"
