3671,"Narrated 'Aishah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Order Abu Bakr to lead the people in Salat."" 'Aishah said: ""O Messenger of Allah! If Abu Bakr takes your place"
3672,"Narrated 'Aishah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""It is not befitting that a group"
3673,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever spends a pair of things in the path of Allah"
3674,"Narrated Zaid bin Aslam:""I heard 'Umar bin Al-Khattab saying: 'We were ordered by the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to give in charity"
3675,Narrated Jubair bin Mut'im:that a woman came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to speak to him about something. Then he ordered her with something
3676,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by Ibn ʿUmayr (may Allah be pleased with both of them):**

He said: ""While we were praying with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), a man from the people said: *'Allāhu Akbar kabīrā* (Allah is the Greatest, greatly), *wal-ḥamdu lillāhi kathīrā* (and praise be to Allah, abundantly), *wa subḥān Allāhi bukratan wa aṣīlā* (and glory be to Allah, morning and evening).""

The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: **""Who said such and such?""** A man from the people said: ""I did, O Messenger of Allah."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: **""I was amazed by it; the gates of the heavens were opened for it.""**

Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with both of them) said: ""I have not abandoned these words since I heard them from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).""

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: ""This is a *ḥasan ṣaḥīh gharīb* hadith from this chain. And al-Ḥajjāj ibn Abī ʿUthmān is al-Ḥajjāj ibn Mayṣara al-Ṣawwāf, and he is known as Abū al-Ṣalt, and he is considered trustworthy (*thiqah*) among the scholars of hadith.""

---

*This hadith is recorded in Sunan al-Tirmidhī and highlights the immense spiritual reward of the remembrance of Allah (dhikr) and the profound significance of glorifying and praising Allah, particularly within the context of prayer.*"
3677,Narrated 'Aishah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) ordered the closing of all the gates
3678,Narrated 'Aishah:that Abu Bakr entered upon the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)
