3687,"Narrated Anas:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""I entered Paradise and it was as if I was in a palace of gold. So I said: 'Whose palace is this?' They said: 'A youth's"
3688,"Narrated Abu Buraidah:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) awoke in the morning and called for Bilal"
3689,"Narrated Buraidah:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went out for one of his expeditions"
3690,Narrated 'Aishah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was sitting and we heard a scream and the voices of children. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) arose
3691,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""I am the first for whom the earth will split"
3692,"Narrated 'Aishah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Among the nations"
3693,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""A man among the inhabitants of Paradise will appear before you."" So Abu Bakr appeared. Then he said: ""A man among the inhabitants of Paradise will appear before you."" So 'Umar appeared"
3694,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""While a man was tending some of his sheep"
3695,Narrated Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him]:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was at Hira
3696,"Narrated by Abu Dawud, Sulayman ibn al-Ash'ath al-Sijistani narrated to us; Qatn al-Basri narrated to us; Ja'far ibn Sulayman reported to us from Thabit, from Anas رضي الله عنه, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:

""Let each one of you ask his Lord for all of his needs, even to the point of asking for the strap of his sandal when it breaks.""

This is a *gharib* (uncommon) Hadith. More than one narrator has transmitted this Hadith from Ja'far ibn Sulayman, from Thabit al-Bunani, from the Prophet ﷺ directly (*marfu'*), without mentioning Anas رضي الله عنه in the chain."
3697,"Salih ibn Abdullah narrated to us, who informed us: Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said:

""Let one of you ask his Lord for his needs, even if it be for salt, or even for the strap of his sandal if it breaks.""

This narration is more authentic than the hadith of Qatan from Ja'far ibn Sulayman."
3698,"Narrated Talhah bin 'Ubaidullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""For every Prophet there is a friend (Rafiq)"
3699,"Narrated Abu 'Abdur-Rahman As-Sulami:""When 'Uthman was besieged"
3700,"Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Khabbab:""I witnessed the Prophet (ﷺ) while he was exhorting support for the 'army of distress.' 'Uthman bin 'Affan stood and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! I will take the responsibility of one-hundred camels"
3701,"Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Samurah:that 'Uthman went to the Prophet (ﷺ) with one-thousand Dinar"" - Al-Hasan bin Waqi (one of the narrators) said: ""And in another place in my book: 'In his garment when the 'army of distress' was being prepared. So he poured them into his lap.'"" - 'Abdur-Rahman said: ""So I saw the Prophet (ﷺ) turning them over in his lap"
3702,Narrated Anas bin Malik:that when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered the pledge of Ridwan
3703,"Narrated Thumamah bin Hazn Al-Qushairi:""I was present at the house when 'Uthman appeared above them saying: 'Bring me your two companions who have gathered you against me.'"" He said: ""So they were brought as if they were two camels"
3704,"Narrated Abu Al-Ash'ath As-Sana'ani:""Some people were delivering Khutbah in Ash-Sham"
3705,"Narrated 'Aishah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""O 'Uthman! Indeed Allah may give you a shirt"
3706,"Narrated 'Uthman bin 'Abdullah bin Mawhab:""A man among the people of Egypt performed Hajj to the House"
3707,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:""While the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was alive"
3708,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) mentioned the Fitnah and said: ""This one will be wrongfully killed during it"
3709,Narrated Jabir:that the Prophet (ﷺ) was brought the body of a deceased man
3710,"Narrated Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari:""I went with the Prophet (ﷺ) and he entered a garden of the Ansar"
3711,"Narrated Abu Sahlah:""The day of the house (when he was besieged)"
3712,Narrated 'Imran bin Husain:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) dispatched an army and he put 'Ali bin Abi Talib in charge of it. He left on the expedition and he entered upon a female slave. So four of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) scolded him
3713,"Narrated to us al-Faḍl ibn Sahl, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aʿraj al-Baghdādī, narrated to us ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ghazwān, Abū Nūḥ, reported to us Yūnus ibn Abī Isḥāq, from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Mūsā, from his father, who said:

Abū Ṭālib set out for Syria, and the Prophet ﷺ accompanied him, along with a group of elders from Quraysh. When they drew near to the monk, they dismounted and began to unpack their saddles. The monk came out to them, although previously they had passed by him and he would not come out to them nor pay them any attention.

He said: While they were unpacking their saddles, the monk moved among them until he came and took the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: ""This is the Master of the worlds. This is the Messenger of the Lord of the worlds. Allah shall send him as a mercy to all the worlds.""

The elders of Quraysh said to him: ""How do you know this?"" He replied: ""When you appeared over the pass, there was no tree or stone that did not fall prostrate, and none prostrate except for a prophet. And I recognize him by the seal of prophethood beneath the cartilage of his shoulder, resembling an apple.""

Then he went back and prepared food for them. When he brought it, the Prophet ﷺ was tending the camels. He said: ""Send for him."" So he came, with a cloud shading him. When he drew near to the people, he found that they had already taken the shade of the tree. When he sat down, the shade of the tree inclined over him. The monk said: ""Look at the shade of the tree, how it has inclined over him.""

He said: While he was standing among them, urging them not to take him to the Romans, for the Romans, if they saw him and recognized him by his description, would kill him — he turned and behold, seven men had arrived from Rome. He went to meet them and said: ""What has brought you?"" They said: ""We have come because this prophet is to emerge in this month, and no road has been left without people being sent to it. We were informed of his news and were dispatched to this road."" He said: ""Is there anyone behind you who is better than you?"" They said: ""We were only informed of his news on this road."" He said: ""Have you considered: if Allah has decreed a matter, can anyone among the people repel it?"" They said: ""No."" He said: ""Then pledge allegiance to him and remain with him.""

He said: ""I adjure you by Allah: who among you is his guardian?"" They said: ""Abū Ṭālib."" So he continued to adjure him until Abū Ṭālib sent him back. Abū Bakr sent Bilāl with him, and the monk provisioned him with bread and oil.

Abū ʿĪsā said: This is a ḥasan gharīb hadith; we do not know it except from this chain."
3714,"Narrated 'Ali bin Abi Talib:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""May Allah have mercy upon Abu Bakr"
3715,"Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Hisham, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, who said: ""The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, passed away at the age of sixty-five."" And thus did he (meaning Ibn Bashnar) narrate it, and Muhammad ibn Isma'il transmitted from him likewise."
3716,"Narrated Al-Bara bin 'Azib:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said to 'Ali bin Abi Talib: ""You are from me"
3717,"Narrated by Muhammad ibn Bashshar and Mahmud ibn Ghaylan, who both reported from Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi, from Sulayman ibn Mu'adh al-Dhabbi, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Indeed, in Mecca there is a stone that used to greet me during the nights of my mission; I recognize it even now."" This is a hasan (good) and gharib (rare) hadith."
3718,"the people of the Ansar, used to recognize the hypocrites, by their hatred for 'Ali bin Abi Talib. \nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 3717 Arabic Hadees: 3717"""
3719,"Narrated Buraidah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed Allah has ordered me to love four"
3720,"Narrated Hubshi bin Junadah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""'Ali is from me and I am from 'Ali. And none should represent me except myself or 'Ali"
3721,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) made bonds of brotherhood among his Companions. So 'Ali came crying saying: ""O Messenger of Allah! You have made a bond of brotherhood among your Companions"
3722,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:""There was a bird with the Prophet (ﷺ)"
3723,"Narrated 'Ali:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""I am the house of wisdom"
